---
// "Below, deeper, earlier" — the quiet engine of the method, for everyone.
// A thin oscillation-wave band (svhgpt-08) leads into the descent image
// (svhgpt-07: a figure rooted down to a single ember). Content from the
// "For everyone" closing of the SVH document.
---

<!-- Thin breathing band -->
<section class="wn-band wn-band--thin">
  <div class="wn-band-bg" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.26" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src="/media/library/svhgpt-08-oscillation-breath-rhythm.webp" alt="" />
  </div>
  <div class="wn-band-inner">
    <p class="wn-band-quote wn-reveal" style="font-size: clamp(22px,3vw,38px);">
      One quiet question, asked patiently: <em>what is below that?</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wn-deeper">
  <div class="wn-deeper-inner">
    <div class="wn-deeper-media wn-reveal" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.15">
      <img src="/media/library/svhgpt-07-below-deeper-earlier.webp" alt="A seated figure whose roots descend through the earth to a single ember of light" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="wn-deeper-text wn-reveal">
      <div class="we-eyebrow">Below, deeper, earlier</div>
      <h2 class="wn-deeper-h2">Almost every fear grows from <em>one root.</em></h2>
      <p>
        Asked patiently beneath any wound, that one question travels below,
        further, deeper, earlier — and tends to arrive at a single core:
        <strong>separation</strong>, the belief that we're cut off from everything
        else. And below separation, when enough attention has been paid to the
        pain, there is joy, oneness, love.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is emphatically not a bypass. The pain must be felt; the injustice
        acknowledged. The deeper layer only reveals itself <em>after</em> the
        foundation is laid — and it arrives by itself.
      </p>
      <p class="wn-deeper-pull">
        In the unchangeable, faith isn't hope. It's the surrender of hitting rock
        bottom and still saying <em>yes</em> to being here. That yes is sacred.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
